Changelog: 02-11-2026 16:54:42

Release 0.2.1.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 16:05:54

Fixed. When Open-Meteo is busy or down (429, 502, 503 or 504) the Weather card says it is unavailable for now, with
Open-Meteo's own reason (503: The service is overloaded) instead of the bare HTTP status, and that it asks again in 30
minutes. Until then the Weather tile on the screen says unavailable now when it has no weather yet, and keeps the last
weather it had otherwise. A tile's caption is cut short with an ellipsis where it would run into the detail beside it
(a long place name).

Changelog: 02-11-2026 14:09:45

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 02:27:11

Release 0.1.0.

Changelog: 02-11-2026 02:04:49

Added. Smart Screen, the BC250 suite's USB IPS3.5 made for the handheld: the handheld's live values on a Turzx USB IPS
screen (the Turing Smart Screen 3.5" and the UsbMonitor 3.5", 5" and 7"), with the time, the date and the weather,
in six themes or your own colors. The screen's protocol, the link that sends only what changed, the reset at the
first connection, the drawing and the weather are the BC250 app's; Windows gives the screen its in-box usbser
driver, so the app finds it as a COM port (by its USB ID and the port name in its Device Parameters) and needs no
driver and no administrator. The values are Windows': the temperatures, the chip's power and the GPU's load from
AMD's driver (core's chip.py), the CPU's clock, the network, the disks and the GPU's load without AMD's driver from
Windows' performance counters by their English names, the memory and the battery; the board's fan, VRM, NVMe and
VRAM tiles gave way to Power and Battery. Six cards: Screen (brightness, orientation, backlight, the picture and a
report saved to Pictures and Documents), Values, Look (theme, four colors from a palette, the header's text on a
page with the touch keyboard, a background picture chosen in core's browser), Clock (the time zone as its offset:
Windows' zone names are too long), Weather (Open-Meteo, searched on a page with the touch keyboard) and Start (start
with Windows minimized through a shortcut in the Startup folder, the screen dark or not when the app closes, run in
the background, the log). The picture the screen shows is beside the panes, as large as the room allows: the whole
height standing, the screen's own 480 x 320 lying down. The screen's header text starts as the
handheld's family (ROG XBOX Ally X). Tried on the owner's Turing 3.5" through the Ally X's dock (COM3, 02-11-2026):
the reset, the connection and a full picture in 1.8 s, as on the BC-250.
